 "note": "The eastern badlands kit's adapter onto the material library (core/materials/PLAN.md, Eastern badlands). leaf.* replace the kit's procedural leaf textures when the page carries this pack (the showcase; the open world loads the kit without it and keeps the procedural ones): keep 0 is a grey detail map the kit's per-instance species colour colours, so one card serves every species on that item. leaf.spray and leaf.weep are cut from one cell or column of their sheet in 50-biome-ebadlands-species.js. ground.* are the showcase host's ground layers (45-host-stage.js), blended per vertex by zone: keep 0 multiplies the painted ground colour by the set's relief, keep 1 shows the set's own colour (sulphur, the acid pools). Run python3 tools/textures/pack.py biomes/ebadlands after any change, then python3 build.py. bark.* and wood.silver replace the bark buckets' canvases (keep 0: the species' vertex colours colour them; mean 0.6, which means() divides out); bark.aspen is the hyperjungle's ghostwood, tinted. stone.gem (stone.amazonite) is the ember crown's pods, full colour. groundDetail and groundCrack (2026-10-06, late): the host's ground layers multiplied over the painted ground (45-host-stage.js hostGroundLib), grey and bright (mean .9; cracks .95 with contrast 1.8), colour map only. (2026-10-06, late) litter: card.litter (one cell); bark.alien (the alien-skin bark, LIBBARK slot 5): skin.alien.banded.",
